    "sentence_translations": [
      "Monkey Year Horse Month",
      "",
      "“Monkey Year Horse Month” is a proverb which usually refers to an unknown point in time long before or after now.",
      "It is also used to refer to something that is unlikely to ever complete.",
      "You can use it like this: “These things all happened a long time ago, how come you still remember?”",
      "Or if someone asks you when you can go on a date with him but you don't want to go, then you can reply like this:",
      "“When Hell freezes over.”",
      "That person will surely understand that you do not want to date him.",
      "",
      "Lately however, you must use this proverb with care, because Monkey Year Horse Month is about to arrive.",
      "Everyone knows that this year 2016 is the Year of the Monkey, and from June 5th to July 3rd is is the Month of the Horse.",
      "So from June 5th to July 3rd 2016 it is Monkey Year Horse Month.",
      "If you said “Wait until Monkey Year Horse Month and I'll go on a date with you”, then you must be careful."
    ]
